+## D9 — Separate lesson counts and content-address public exports
+
+**Choice.** Keep one fixed depth per episode, expose independent demonstration/query counts, retain the bounded support `1..8` for each with at most 12 total pairs, and use the retained 3-demo/4-query command. Public artifacts are canonical visible bytes named by their SHA-256; duplicate visible payloads fail rather than overwrite.
+
+**Rationale.** Four rotations of one hidden query are not four-query supervision, and ordinal filenames tied to consecutive seed-selected settings expose private construction order. Content-derived IDs make the public projection reproducible without incorporating settings, seeds, programs, or query answers.
